# Live experiment output is NOT git-tracked, deliberately.
#
# It was, briefly, because `git add -f <dossier>` swept the whole directory in. A branch switch
# then deleted score CSVs and the driver script out from under a RUNNING job — and bash reads
# scripts incrementally, so removing a running script can kill the run outright. Nothing was lost
# (it was committed), but the hazard is real and the fix is to not track output while it is being
# written. Results are curated into the dossier's markdown; the raw CSVs stay local.
*
!.gitignore
